  --num_prepend_vtokens NUM_PREPEND_VTOKENS [NUM_PREPEND_VTOKENS ...]
                        Number of (default) virtual tokens to prepend to each
                        sentence. For example, '--num_prepend_vtokens=10' will
                        prepend the tokens [vocab_size, vocab_size + 1, ...,
                        vocab_size + 9] to the sentence.
  --draft_target_model_config DRAFT_TARGET_MODEL_CONFIG
                        Configuration of Draft-Target-Model decoding, see
                        `examples/draft_target_model/README.md` for more
                        information. E.g.: [4, [0], [1], False] for
                        [draft_len, draft_model_device_list,
                        target_model_device_list, use_logits].
  --prompt_lookup_config PROMPT_LOOKUP_CONFIG
                        Configuration of Prompt-Lookup decoding, see
                        `examples/prompt_lookup/README.md` for more
                        information. E.g.: [10,2,[0]] for
                        [prompt_lookup_num_tokens, max_matching_ngram_size,
                        device_list].
  --medusa_choices MEDUSA_CHOICES
                        Configuration of Medusa decoding. E.g.: [[0, 0, 0, 0],
                        [0, 1, 0], [1, 0], [1, 1]] for 9 medusa tokens.
  --eagle_choices EAGLE_CHOICES
                        Configuration of Eagle-1 decoding. E.g.: [[0, 0, 0,
                        0], [0, 1, 0], [1, 0], [1, 1]] for 9 draft tokens.
  --eagle_posterior_threshold EAGLE_POSTERIOR_THRESHOLD
                        Minimum token probability threshold for typical
                        acceptance. Enables typical acceptance in Eagle.
                        Corresponds to epsilon in
                        https://arxiv.org/pdf/2401.10774.
  --eagle_use_dynamic_tree
                        Whether to use Ealge-2
  --eagle_dynamic_tree_max_top_k EAGLE_DYNAMIC_TREE_MAX_TOP_K
                        The maximum number of draft tokens to expand for each
                        node in Eagle-2.
  --lookahead_config LOOKAHEAD_CONFIG
                        Configuration of executor and request lookahead
                        decoding. E.g.: [5, 6, 7] for [max_window_size,
                        max_ngram_size, max_verification_set_size].
  --engine_dir ENGINE_DIR
  --tokenizer_type TOKENIZER_TYPE
                        Specify that argument when providing a .model file as
                        the tokenizer_dir. It allows AutoTokenizer to
                        instantiate the correct tokenizer type.
  --vocab_file VOCAB_FILE
                        Used for sentencepiece tokenizers
  --no_add_special_tokens
                        Whether or not to add special tokens
  --hf_model_dir HF_MODEL_DIR, --model_dir HF_MODEL_DIR
  --tokenizer_dir TOKENIZER_DIR
                        tokenizer path; defaults to hf_model_dir if left
                        unspecified
  --gpu_weights_percent GPU_WEIGHTS_PERCENT
                        Specify the percentage of weights that reside on GPU
                        instead of CPU and streaming load during runtime.
  --max_tokens_in_paged_kv_cache MAX_TOKENS_IN_PAGED_KV_CACHE
                        Specify the maximum number of tokens in a kv cache
                        page (only available with cpp session).
  --kv_cache_enable_block_reuse, --no-kv_cache_enable_block_reuse
                        Enables block reuse in kv cache (only available with
                        cpp session).
  --kv_cache_free_gpu_memory_fraction KV_CACHE_FREE_GPU_MEMORY_FRACTION
                        Specify the free gpu memory fraction.
  --cross_kv_cache_fraction CROSS_KV_CACHE_FRACTION
                        Specify the kv cache fraction reserved for cross
                        attention. Only applicable for encoder-decoder models.
                        By default 0.5 for self and 0.5 for cross.
  --enable_chunked_context
                        Enables chunked context (only available with cpp
                        session).
  --hf_data_type {fp32,fp16,bf16,float32,float16,bfloat16}, --data_type {fp32,fp16,bf16,float32,float16,bfloat16}
                        The data type for hf model.
  --hf_device_map_auto  Use device map 'auto' to load a pretrained HF model.
                        This may help to test a large model that cannot fit
